# Changelog

## v0.1.0

- {{name}} extracts verbatim statement challenges and bundles requested roots.
- Definition-hole bodies are displayed verbatim, with Comparator's exclusion
  labeled and a separate proof-erasure comparison against handmade bodies.
- Explicit unsafe roots are refused before export and tested as refusals.
- Nanoda replay remains enabled by default; `--no-nanoda` explicitly records a
  skipped replay while retaining strict comparison, axiom checks and Lean replay.
- Metrics include physical and nonblank lines and raw generated constants.
- Includes deletion tests, negative controls, proof-erasure fixtures and pinned
  ten-proofs comparisons with byte-for-byte reproduction.
- Core CI runs on Ubuntu; the manual example job builds only the Ramsey module.
  Actual run outcomes are recorded separately, without claiming arbitrary-input
  minimality, intended statement meaning or an adversarial sandbox.
